		<title type="html"><![CDATA[Re: COM Ports Error]]></title>

		
		<content type="html" xml:base="http://localhost/opengd77/viewtopic.php?t=5139&amp;p=37250#p37250"><![CDATA[
I had no problems when I used another Laptop, I was able to update the firmware and data base.  <br>The same problem popped up on the FB group and the<br>reply was posted.<br><br>I was able to resolve the issue with the following steps: (spoiler alert: It was not discoverable as a Com port device until AFTER it was flashed.)<br>Full un-install of the OpenGD77 CPS<br>Regedt32 as admin<br>Edit: Find: VID_15A2&amp;PID_0073 (Under Devices, HID Devices, Properties, Details, Hardware Ids (and confirmed with a linux machine for the USB connection to the radio)<br>Delete all the keys with that info in them.<br>Edit: Find: opengd77<br>Delete all the keys with that info<br>reboot the PC<br>Install the OpenGD77 CPS software, allowing driver as Admin.<br>Without running the CPS, I re-connected the radio both in normal and DFU modes.<br>No Change in discovering hardware. (Still HID Device)<br>Turned off and disconnected radio<br>Connected cable to radio, Turn on in DFU Mode.<br>Connect to USB<br>Opened OpenGD77 CPS as Admin.<br>Select Extras, Firmware Loader,<br>Click "Select official firmware (donor) file"<br>Select the GD-77_V4.3.6.sgl<br>Click "Select a File &amp; Update"<br>Select OpenGD770513.zip<br>It FINALLY was able to find and upload to the radio.<br>After completion, it rebooted the radio, and now it is found as OpenGD77 (Com3)<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=6541">VK3TV</a> — Tue May 27, 2025 10:39 pm</p><hr />
]]></content>
